    {
      "id": 11,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Refusals by bound — ceiling vs reserve",
      "description": "Which limit actually decided the refusal. bound=ceiling: the tenant's own undelivered-command ceiling would have refused this anyway. bound=reserve: it fitted against the raw ceiling and was refused ONLY by the delivery-machinery reserve — that is the counterfactual, not merely \"a reserve was in force\", so this series names refusals the reserve genuinely caused. bound=none: a refusal that was never about a limit. Tune the ceiling or the reserve when the reserve line is standing rather than spiking.",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
