    {
      "id": 14,
      "type": "stat",
      "title": "Claims STRANDED /s — commands that will lie",
      "description": "🔴 THE ONE TO LOOK AT FIRST. A stranded claim is a command left reading SENT whose publish failed AND whose release failed too. It was never sent, nothing will retry it, and it will expire as TIMEOUT — blaming a device that did nothing wrong. Every other counter on this page describes something that reported itself; this one describes the platform telling an operator something false. Any non-zero value deserves investigation. Alerted as CommandClaimsStranded (critical).",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 4,
        "w": 8,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 30
      },
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${datasource}"
      },
